  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is re-engineering established analysis steps for throughput and storage efficiency rather than introducing new analytical paradigms. deepTools4 rewrites its core functions with benchmarked speed-ups. RapidGLM provides a C++ library reported to accelerate count-regression differential expression, CRISPR-screen and eQTL analyses 2.5–17.8x. pbzarr stores per-base data for thousands of samples in Zarr and is reported to be faster and smaller than D4 and bigWig. CyteArc supports out-of-core single-cell multi-omic analysis beyond 100M cells. MAUDE-Py ports a sorting-screen framework to Python, and CATEomics adds model selection and ensembling for CATE estimation on omics data. A parallel thread is precomputed or uniformly reprocessed resources. Evo2VED serves Evo2 variant-effect scores for 6.48M gnomAD variants. The Biodiversity Cell Atlas reprocesses 39 single-cell atlases across 33 species. GI-DB and the CNCB-NGDC update extend population and database coverage, and a haploblock-hash dataset covers 2,548 1000 Genomes individuals. Breedbase integrates breeding-program statistics.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
